      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T08:15:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems a bit inconsistent that the error would have a transactionId if the service type was invalid, but would not if it\u0027s because of FAILURE_MAX_LIMIT.\n\nI\u0027m thinking the transactionId should only be there if a transaction was actually submitted; which would be the same case as the error having a non-zero duration.\n\nSo you could have: `clientInfo.onRegisterServiceFailedImmediately(int requestId, int errorCode)`, which ends up logging 0 for the duration and some placeholder transactionId; and `clientInfo.onRegisterServiceFailed(int requestId, int errorCode, int transactionId, long durationMs)`.\n\nThat would make it easier to identify the cases where the registration wasn\u0027t even attempted in the metrics.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 862,
        "startChar": 75,
        "endLine": 862,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "74ae8ae7c1ecb06003cb315cecd187338da2ad7b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
